Subject: Fix blank screen on Qt 6.10: 'char' is a reserved word

Qt 6.10 (Fedora 43) rejects 'required property string char' with
"Unexpected token 'reserved word'". PasswordInput.qml fails to load, which
takes Lock.qml and Shell.qml down with it, so the whole shell never starts.
Use the model object instead, like Input.qml and Dropdown.qml already do.

--- a/src/quickshell/reusables/PasswordInput.qml	2026-09-22 11:13:03.729733662 +0700
+++ b/src/quickshell/reusables/PasswordInput.qml	2026-09-22 11:13:03.730957953 +0700
@@ -804,7 +804,7 @@
                 delegate: Item {
                     id: charSlot
                     required property int index
-                    required property string char
+                    required property var model
 
                     property real baseWidth: root.charSlotWidth > 0
                         ? root.charSlotWidth
@@ -862,7 +862,7 @@
                     Text {
                         id: charText
                         anchors.centerIn: parent
-                        text: charSlot.char
+                        text: charSlot.model.char
                         color: root.textColor
 
                         font.family: root.fontFamily
